# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which means a fresh clone would get a
# CRLF working tree while the repo stores LF. That is normally harmless, but
# this project commits a GENERATED file: tools/build.mjs --check rebuilds
# splitcraft.html from src/ and compares it byte-for-byte against the copy on
# disk, and tests/run.mjs builds before every run. Any line-ending asymmetry
# between the sources and the built artefact makes that comparison fail for
# reasons that have nothing to do with the code — the worst kind of "works on
# my machine", because it only appears in a fresh clone.
#
# Pinning eol=lf keeps the working tree matching what is committed, on every
# platform, which is also what the files already are today.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary

# splitcraft.html is built from src/ by tools/build.mjs. Marking it generated
# collapses it in diffs and keeps it out of language statistics, so a one-line
# source change doesn't show up as a 400KB diff burying the actual edit.
splitcraft.html linguist-generated=true
